Key Intelligence Topics (KITs) and Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs) may be further subdivided to focus on political, economic, diplomatic, military, financial, or intellectual property categories.  An adversary may specify KITs or KIQs in this manner in order to understand how the information they are pursuing can have multiple uses and to consider all aspects of the types of information they need to target for a particular purpose.  KIT." tabindex="0" aria-label="T1229">Assess KITs/KIQs benefits</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assign KITs, KIQs, and/or intelligence requirements - T1238&quot;" data-cluster-id="16373" title="T1238: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Once generated, Key Intelligence Topics (KITs), Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs), and/or intelligence requirements are assigned to applicable agencies and/or personnel. For example, an adversary may decide nuclear energy requirements should be assigned to a specific organization based on their mission.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1238">Assign KITs, KIQs, and/or intelligence requirements</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine approach/attack vector - T1245&quot;" data-cluster-id="16841" title="T1245: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The approach or attack vector outlines the specifics behind how the adversary would like to attack the target.  As additional information is known through the other phases of PRE-ATT&amp;CK, an adversary may update the approach or attack vector.     " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1245">Determine approach/attack vector</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire OSINT data sets and information - T1247&quot;" data-cluster-id="16408" title="T1247: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Open source intelligence (OSINT) is intelligence gathered from publicly available sources. This can include both information gathered on-line, such as from search engines, as well as in the physical world. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1247">Acquire OSINT data sets and information</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire OSINT data sets and information - T1266&quot;" data-cluster-id="16409" title="T1266: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Open source intelligence (OSINT) provides free, readily available information about a target while providing the target no indication they are of interest.  Such information can assist an adversary in crafting a successful approach for compromise. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1266">Acquire OSINT data sets and information</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire OSINT data sets and information - T1277&quot;" data-cluster-id="16410" title="T1277: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Data sets can be anything from Security Exchange Commission (SEC) filings to public phone numbers. Many datasets are now either publicly available for free or can be purchased from a variety of data vendors.  Open source intelligence (OSINT) is intelligence gathered from publicly available sources. This can include both information gathered on-line as well as in the physical world.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1277">Acquire OSINT data sets and information</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze application security posture - T1293&quot;" data-cluster-id="16625" title="T1293: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can probe a victim&#039;s network to determine configurations. The configurations may provide opportunities to route traffic through the network in an undetected or less detectable way.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1293">Analyze application security posture</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies - T1297&quot;" data-cluster-id="16470" title="T1297: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Understanding organizational skillsets and deficiencies could provide insight in to weakness in defenses, or opportunities for exploitation. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1297">Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze business processes - T1301&quot;" data-cluster-id="16868" title="T1301: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Business processes, such as who typically communicates with who, or what the supply chain is for a particular part, provide opportunities for social engineering or other  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1301">Analyze business processes</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire and/or use 3rd party infrastructure services - T1307&quot;" data-cluster-id="16361" title="T1307: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A wide variety of cloud, virtual private services, hosting, compute, and storage solutions are available. Additionally botnets are available for rent or purchase. Use of these solutions allow an adversary to stage, launch, and execute an attack from infrastructure that does not physically tie back to them and can be rapidly provisioned, modified, and shut down. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1307">Acquire and/or use 3rd party infrastructure services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire and/or use 3rd party infrastructure services - T1329&quot;" data-cluster-id="16364" title="T1329: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A wide variety of cloud, virtual private services, hosting, compute, and storage solutions are available. Additionally botnets are available for rent or purchase. Use of these solutions allow an adversary to stage, launch, and execute an attack from infrastructure that does not physically tie back to them and can be rapidly provisioned, modified, and shut down. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1329">Acquire and/or use 3rd party infrastructure services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Build social network persona - T1341&quot;" data-cluster-id="16607" title="T1341: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

For attacks incorporating social engineering the utilization of an on-line persona is important. These personas may be fictitious or impersonate real people. The persona may exist on a single site or across multiple sites (Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Google+, etc.).   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1341">Build social network persona</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Build and configure delivery systems - T1347&quot;" data-cluster-id="16479" title="T1347: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Delivery systems are the infrastructure used by the adversary to host malware or other tools used during exploitation. Building and configuring delivery systems may include multiple activities such as registering domain names, renting hosting space, or configuring previously exploited environments. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1347">Build and configure delivery systems</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Review logs and residual traces - T1358&quot;" data-cluster-id="16485" title="T1358: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Execution of code and network communications often result in logging or other system or network forensic artifacts. An adversary can run their code to identify what is recorded under different conditions. This may result in changes to their code or adding additional actions (such as deleting a record from a log) to the code.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1358">Review logs and residual traces</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Disseminate removable media - T1379&quot;" data-cluster-id="17014" title="T1379: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Removable media containing malware can be injected in to a supply chain at large or small scale. It can also be physically placed for someone to find or can be sent to someone in a more targeted manner. The intent is to have the user utilize the removable media on a system where the adversary is trying to gain access.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1379">Disseminate removable media</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Authentication attempt - T1381&quot;" data-cluster-id="17400" title="T1381: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Attempt to use default vendor credentials, brute force credentials, or previously obtained legitimate credentials to authenticate remotely. This access could be to a web portal, through a VPN, or in a phone app.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1381">Authentication attempt</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Authorized user performs requested cyber action - T1386&quot;" data-cluster-id="16418" title="T1386: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Clicking on links in email, opening attachments, or visiting websites that result in drive by downloads can all result in compromise due to users performing actions of a cyber nature. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1386">Authorized user performs requested cyber action</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess current holdings, needs, and wants - T1236&quot;" data-cluster-id="16374" title="T1236: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analysts assess current information available against requirements that outline needs and wants as part of the research baselining process to begin satisfying a requirement.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1236">Assess current holdings, needs, and wants</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Receive KITs/KIQs and determine requirements - T1239&quot;" data-cluster-id="16442" title="T1239: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Applicable agencies and/or personnel receive intelligence requirements and evaluate them to determine sub-requirements related to topics, questions, or requirements.  For example, an adversary&#039;s  nuclear energy requirements may be further divided into nuclear facilities versus nuclear warhead capabilities. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1239">Receive KITs/KIQs and determine requirements</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine highest level tactical element - T1243&quot;" data-cluster-id="16465" title="T1243: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

From a tactical viewpoint, an adversary could potentially have a primary and secondary level target.  The primary target represents the highest level tactical element the adversary wishes to attack.  For example, the corporate network within a corporation or the division within an agency.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1243">Determine highest level tactical element</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct active scanning - T1254&quot;" data-cluster-id="16977" title="T1254: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Active scanning is the act of sending transmissions to end nodes, and analyzing the responses, in order to identify information about the communications system. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1254">Conduct active scanning</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Aggregate individual&#039;s digital footprint - T1275&quot;" data-cluster-id="16500" title="T1275: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

In addition to a target&#039;s social media presence may exist a larger digital footprint, such as accounts and credentials on e-commerce sites or usernames and logins for email.  An adversary familiar with a target&#039;s username can mine to determine the target&#039;s larger digital footprint via publicly available sources.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1275">Aggregate individual&#039;s digital footprint</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct social engineering - T1279&quot;" data-cluster-id="16995" title="T1279: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Social Engineering is the practice of manipulating people in order to get them to divulge information or take an action.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1279">Conduct social engineering</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze architecture and configuration posture - T1288&quot;" data-cluster-id="16471" title="T1288: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary may analyze technical scanning results to identify weaknesses in the configuration or architecture of a victim network. These weaknesses could include  architectural flaws, misconfigurations, or improper security controls. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1288">Analyze architecture and configuration posture</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze social and business relationships, interests, and affiliations - T1295&quot;" data-cluster-id="16355" title="T1295: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Social media provides insight into the target&#039;s affiliations with groups and organizations.  Certification information can explain their technical associations and professional associations. Personal information can provide data for exploitation or even blackmail. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1295">Analyze social and business relationships, interests, and affiliations</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies - T1300&quot;" data-cluster-id="16448" title="T1300: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analyze strengths and weaknesses of the target for potential areas of where to focus compromise efforts. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1300">Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire and/or use 3rd party software services - T1308&quot;" data-cluster-id="16362" title="T1308: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A wide variety of 3rd party software services  are available (e.g., Twitter, Dropbox, GoogleDocs). Use of these solutions allow an adversary to stage, launch, and execute an attack from infrastructure that does not physically tie back to them and can be rapidly provisioned, modified, and shut down.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1308">Acquire and/or use 3rd party software services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire and/or use 3rd party software services - T1330&quot;" data-cluster-id="16360" title="T1330: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A wide variety of 3rd party software services  are available (e.g., Twitter, Dropbox, GoogleDocs). Use of these solutions allow an adversary to stage, launch, and execute an attack from infrastructure that does not physically tie back to them and can be rapidly provisioned, modified, and shut down. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1330">Acquire and/or use 3rd party software services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Choose pre-compromised mobile app developer account credentials or signing keys - T1391&quot;" data-cluster-id="16352" title="T1391: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The adversary can use account credentials or signing keys of an existing mobile app developer to publish malicious updates of existing mobile apps to an application store, or to abuse the developer&#039;s identity and reputation to publish new malicious apps.  Many mobile devices are configured to automatically install new versions of already-installed apps. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1391">Choose pre-compromised mobile app developer account credentials or signing keys</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Build or acquire exploits - T1349&quot;" data-cluster-id="16643" title="T1349: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An exploit takes advantage of a bug or vulnerability in order to cause unintended or unanticipated behavior to occur on computer hardware or software. The adversary may use or modify existing exploits when those exploits are still relevant to the environment they are trying to compromise.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1349">Build or acquire exploits</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test ability to evade automated mobile application security analysis performed by app stores - T1393&quot;" data-cluster-id="16351" title="T1393: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Many mobile devices are configured to only allow applications to be installed from the mainstream vendor app stores (e.g., Apple App Store and Google Play Store). An adversary can submit multiple code samples to these stores deliberately designed to probe the stores&#039; security analysis capabilities, with the goal of determining effective techniques to place malicious applications in the stores that could then be delivered to targeted devices.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1393">Test ability to evade automated mobile application security analysis performed by app stores</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Distribute malicious software development tools - T1394&quot;" data-cluster-id="16483" title="T1394: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary could distribute malicious software development tools (e.g., compiler) that hide malicious behavior in software built using the tools.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1394">Distribute malicious software development tools</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct social engineering or HUMINT operation - T1376&quot;" data-cluster-id="16416" title="T1376: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Social Engineering is the practice of manipulating people in order to get them to divulge information or take an action. Human Intelligence (HUMINT) is intelligence collected and provided by human sources.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1376">Conduct social engineering or HUMINT operation</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Automated system performs requested action - T1384&quot;" data-cluster-id="16480" title="T1384: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Users may be performing legitimate activity but using media that is compromised (e.g., using a USB drive that comes with malware installed during manufacture or supply). Upon insertion in the system the media auto-runs and the malware executes without further action by the user. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1384">Automated system performs requested action</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess leadership areas of interest - T1224&quot;" data-cluster-id="16463" title="T1224: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership assesses the areas of most interest to them and generates Key Intelligence Topics (KIT) or Key Intelligence Questions (KIQ). For example, an adversary knows from open and closed source reporting that cyber is of interest, resulting in it being a KIT. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1224">Assess leadership areas of interest</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Submit KITs, KIQs, and intelligence requirements - T1237&quot;" data-cluster-id="16375" title="T1237: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Once they have been created, intelligence requirements, Key Intelligence Topics (KITs), and Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs) are submitted into a central management system.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1237">Submit KITs, KIQs, and intelligence requirements</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine operational element - T1242&quot;" data-cluster-id="16958" title="T1242: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

If going from strategic down to tactical or vice versa, an  adversary would next consider the operational element.  For example, the specific company within an industry or agency within a government.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1242">Determine operational element</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct passive scanning - T1253&quot;" data-cluster-id="16969" title="T1253: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Passive scanning is the act of looking at existing network traffic in order to identify information about the communications system.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1253">Conduct passive scanning</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct social engineering - T1268&quot;" data-cluster-id="16992" title="T1268: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Social Engineering is the practice of manipulating people in order to get them to divulge information or take an action.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1268">Conduct social engineering</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine 3rd party infrastructure services - T1284&quot;" data-cluster-id="16464" title="T1284: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A wide variety of cloud, virtual private services, hosting, compute, and storage solutions are available as 3rd party infrastructure services. These services could provide an adversary with another avenue of approach or compromise.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1284">Determine 3rd party infrastructure services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze data collected - T1287&quot;" data-cluster-id="16994" title="T1287: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary will assess collected information such as software/hardware versions, vulnerabilities, patch level, etc.  They will analyze technical scanning results to identify weaknesses in the confirmation or architecture.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1287">Analyze data collected</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess targeting options - T1296&quot;" data-cluster-id="16993" title="T1296: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary may assess a target&#039;s operational security (OPSEC) practices in order to identify targeting options. A target may share different information in different settings or be more of less cautious in different environments.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1296">Assess targeting options</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze presence of outsourced capabilities - T1303&quot;" data-cluster-id="16452" title="T1303: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Outsourcing, the arrangement of one company providing goods or services to another company for something that could be done in-house, provides another avenue for an adversary to target. Businesses often have networks, portals, or other technical connections between themselves and their outsourced/partner organizations that could be exploited. Additionally, outsourced/partner organization information could provide opportunities for phishing.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1303">Analyze presence of outsourced capabilities</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire or compromise 3rd party signing certificates - T1310&quot;" data-cluster-id="16365" title="T1310: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Code signing is the process of digitally signing executables or scripts to confirm the software author and guarantee that the code has not been altered or corrupted. Users may trust a signed piece of code more than an unsigned piece of code even if they don&#039;t know who issued the certificate or who the author is. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1310">Acquire or compromise 3rd party signing certificates</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Acquire or compromise 3rd party signing certificates - T1332&quot;" data-cluster-id="16367" title="T1332: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Code signing is the process of digitally signing executables and scripts to confirm the software author and guarantee that the code has not been altered or corrupted. Users may trust a signed piece of code more than an unsigned piece of code even if they don&#039;t know who issued the certificate or who the author is. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1332">Acquire or compromise 3rd party signing certificates</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Choose pre-compromised persona and affiliated accounts - T1343&quot;" data-cluster-id="16380" title="T1343: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

For attacks incorporating social engineering the utilization of an on-line persona is important. Utilizing an existing persona with compromised accounts may engender a level of trust in a potential victim if they have a relationship, or knowledge of, the compromised persona.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1343">Choose pre-compromised persona and affiliated accounts</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;C2 protocol development - T1352&quot;" data-cluster-id="16955" title="T1352: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Command and Control (C2 or C&amp;C) is a method by which the adversary communicates with malware. An adversary may use a variety of protocols and methods to execute C2 such as a centralized server, peer to peer, IRC, compromised web sites, or even social media. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1352">C2 protocol development</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test callback functionality - T1356&quot;" data-cluster-id="17009" title="T1356: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Callbacks are malware communications seeking instructions. An adversary will test their malware to ensure the appropriate instructions are conveyed and the callback software can be reached. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1356">Test callback functionality</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Friend/Follow/Connect to targets of interest - T1364&quot;" data-cluster-id="16440" title="T1364: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A form of social engineering designed build trust and to lay the foundation for future interactions or attacks. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1364">Friend/Follow/Connect to targets of interest</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Credential pharming - T1374&quot;" data-cluster-id="17451" title="T1374: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Credential pharming a  form of attack designed to steal users&#039; credential by redirecting users to fraudulent websites. Pharming can be conducted either by changing the hosts file on a victim&#039;s computer or by exploitation of a vulnerability in DNS server software.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1374">Credential pharming</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Compromise of externally facing system - T1388&quot;" data-cluster-id="16489" title="T1388: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Exploit Public-Facing Application and External Remote Services where appropriate.**

Externally facing systems allow connections from outside the network as a normal course of operations.  Externally facing systems may include, but are not limited to, websites, web portals, email, DNS, FTP, VPN concentrators, and boarder routers and firewalls. These systems could be in a demilitarized zone (DMZ) or may be within other parts of the internal environment.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1388">Compromise of externally facing system</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assign KITs/KIQs into categories - T1228&quot;" data-cluster-id="16559" title="T1228: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership organizes Key Intelligence Topics (KITs) and Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs) into three types of categories and creates more if necessary.  An example of a description of key players KIT would be when an adversary assesses the cyber defensive capabilities of a nation-state threat actor. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1228">Assign KITs/KIQs into categories</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Task requirements - T1240&quot;" data-cluster-id="17342" title="T1240: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Once divided into the most granular parts, analysts work with collection managers to task the collection management system with requirements and sub-requirements.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1240">Task requirements</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine secondary level tactical element - T1244&quot;" data-cluster-id="16466" title="T1244: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The secondary level tactical element the adversary seeks to attack is the specific network or area of a network that is vulnerable to attack.  Within the corporate network example, the secondary level tactical element might be a SQL server or a domain controller with a known vulnerability.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1244">Determine secondary level tactical element</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct social engineering - T1249&quot;" data-cluster-id="16982" title="T1249: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Social Engineering is the practice of manipulating people in order to get them to divulge information or take an action.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1249">Conduct social engineering</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify business relationships - T1272&quot;" data-cluster-id="16962" title="T1272: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Business relationship information includes the associates of a target and may be discovered via social media sites such as LinkedIn or public press releases announcing new partnerships between organizations or people (such as key hire announcements in industry articles).  This information may be used by an adversary to shape social engineering attempts (exploiting who a target expects to hear from) or to plan for technical actions such as exploiting network trust relationship.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1272">Identify business relationships</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine centralization of IT management - T1285&quot;" data-cluster-id="16468" title="T1285: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Determining if a &quot;corporate&quot; help desk exists, the degree of access and control it has, and whether there are &quot;edge&quot; units that may have different support processes and standards. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1285">Determine centralization of IT management</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze hardware/software security defensive capabilities - T1294&quot;" data-cluster-id="16444" title="T1294: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can probe a victim&#039;s network to determine configurations. The configurations may provide opportunities to route traffic through the network in an undetected or less detectable way. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1294">Analyze hardware/software security defensive capabilities</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess opportunities created by business deals - T1299&quot;" data-cluster-id="16411" title="T1299: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

During mergers, divestitures, or other period of change in joint infrastructure or business processes there may be an opportunity for exploitation. During this type of churn, unusual requests, or other non standard practices may not be as noticeable.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1299">Assess opportunities created by business deals</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Anonymity services - T1306&quot;" data-cluster-id="17352" title="T1306: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Anonymity services reduce the amount of information available that can be used to track an adversary&#039;s activities.  Multiple options are available to hide activity, limit tracking, and increase anonymity.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1306">Anonymity services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Buy domain name - T1328&quot;" data-cluster-id="16974" title="T1328: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Domain Names are the human readable names used to represent one or more IP addresses. They can be purchased or, in some cases, acquired for free. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1328">Buy domain name</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Develop social network persona digital footprint - T1342&quot;" data-cluster-id="16405" title="T1342: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Both newly built personas and pre-compromised personas may require development of additional documentation to make them seem real. This could include filling out profile information, developing social networks, or incorporating photos.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1342">Develop social network persona digital footprint</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Compromise 3rd party or closed-source vulnerability/exploit information - T1354&quot;" data-cluster-id="16357" title="T1354: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

There is usually a delay between when a vulnerability or exploit is discovered and when it is made public. An adversary may target the systems of those known to research vulnerabilities in order to gain that knowledge for use during a different attack. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1354">Compromise 3rd party or closed-source vulnerability/exploit information</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test malware in various execution environments - T1357&quot;" data-cluster-id="16415" title="T1357: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Malware may perform differently on different platforms (computer vs handheld) and different operating systems (Ubuntu vs OS X), and versions (Windows 7 vs 10) so malicious actors will test their malware in the environment(s) where they most expect it to be executed. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1357">Test malware in various execution environments</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Hardware or software supply chain implant - T1365&quot;" data-cluster-id="16414" title="T1365: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

During production and distribution, the placement of software, firmware, or a CPU chip in a computer, handheld, or other electronic device that enables an adversary to gain illegal entrance.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1365">Hardware or software supply chain implant</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;DNS poisoning - T1382&quot;" data-cluster-id="17435" title="T1382: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

DNS (cache) poisoning is the corruption of an Internet server&#039;s domain name system table by replacing an Internet address with that of another, rogue address. When a Web user seeks the page with that address, the request is redirected by the rogue entry in the table to a different address.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1382">DNS poisoning</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Confirmation of launched compromise achieved - T1383&quot;" data-cluster-id="16476" title="T1383: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Upon successful compromise the adversary may implement methods for confirming success including communication to a command and control server, exfiltration of data, or a verifiable intended effect such as a publicly accessible resource being inaccessible or a web page being defaced.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1383">Confirmation of launched compromise achieved</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Conduct cost/benefit analysis - T1226&quot;" data-cluster-id="16839" title="T1226: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership conducts a cost/benefit analysis that generates a compelling need for information gathering which triggers a Key Intelligence Toptic (KIT) or Key Intelligence Question (KIQ). For example, an adversary compares the cost of cyber intrusions with the expected benefits from increased intelligence collection on cyber adversaries.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1226">Conduct cost/benefit analysis</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine strategic target - T1241&quot;" data-cluster-id="16927" title="T1241: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary undergoes an iterative target selection process that may begin either broadly and narrow down into specifics (strategic to tactical) or narrowly and expand outward (tactical to strategic).  As part of this process, an adversary may determine a high level target they wish to attack. One example of this may be a particular country, government, or commercial sector.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1241">Determine strategic target</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine 3rd party infrastructure services - T1260&quot;" data-cluster-id="16451" title="T1260: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Infrastructure services includes the hardware, software, and network resources required to operate a communications environment. This infrastructure can be managed by a 3rd party rather than being managed by the owning organization.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1260">Determine 3rd party infrastructure services</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify groups/roles - T1270&quot;" data-cluster-id="17282" title="T1270: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Personnel internally to a company may belong to a group or maintain a role with  electronic specialized access, authorities, or privilege that make them an attractive target for an adversary.  One example of this is a system administrator. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1270">Identify groups/roles</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine physical locations - T1282&quot;" data-cluster-id="16963" title="T1282: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Physical locality information may be used by an adversary to shape social engineering attempts (language, culture, events, weather, etc.) or to plan for physical actions such as dumpster diving or attempting to access a facility. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1282">Determine physical locations</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies - T1289&quot;" data-cluster-id="16472" title="T1289: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analyze strengths and weaknesses of the target for potential areas of where to focus compromise efforts. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1289">Analyze organizational skillsets and deficiencies</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess security posture of physical locations - T1302&quot;" data-cluster-id="16398" title="T1302: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Physical access may be required for certain types of adversarial actions.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1302">Assess security posture of physical locations</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Common, high volume protocols and software - T1321&quot;" data-cluster-id="16376" title="T1321: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Certain types of traffic (e.g., Twitter14, HTTP) are more commonly used than others. Utilizing more common protocols and software may make an adversary&#039;s traffic more difficult to distinguish from legitimate traffic. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1321">Common, high volume protocols and software</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Compromise 3rd party infrastructure to support delivery - T1334&quot;" data-cluster-id="16368" title="T1334: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Instead of buying, leasing, or renting infrastructure an adversary may compromise infrastructure and use it for some or all of the attack cycle.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1334">Compromise 3rd party infrastructure to support delivery</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Friend/Follow/Connect to targets of interest - T1344&quot;" data-cluster-id="16439" title="T1344: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Once a persona has been developed an adversary will use it to create connections to targets of interest. These connections may be direct or may include trying to connect through others.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1344">Friend/Follow/Connect to targets of interest</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Create custom payloads - T1345&quot;" data-cluster-id="17001" title="T1345: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A payload is the part of the malware which performs a malicious action. The adversary may create custom payloads when none exist with the needed capability or when targeting a specific environment. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1345">Create custom payloads</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test malware to evade detection - T1359&quot;" data-cluster-id="16487" title="T1359: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can run their code on systems with cyber security protections, such as antivirus products, in place to see if their code is detected. They can also test their malware on freely available public services. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1359">Test malware to evade detection</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Port redirector - T1363&quot;" data-cluster-id="17449" title="T1363: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Redirecting a communication request from one address and port number combination to another. May be set up to obfuscate the final location of communications that will occur in later stages of an attack. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1363">Port redirector</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Deploy exploit using advertising - T1380&quot;" data-cluster-id="16581" title="T1380: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Exploits spread through advertising (malvertising) involve injecting malicious or malware-laden advertisements into legitimate online advertising networks and webpages. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1380">Deploy exploit using advertising</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Human performs requested action of physical nature - T1385&quot;" data-cluster-id="16369" title="T1385: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Through social engineering or other methods, an adversary can get users to perform physical actions that provide access to an adversary.  This could include providing a password over the phone or inserting a &#039;found&#039; CD or USB into a system.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1385">Human performs requested action of physical nature</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Create implementation plan - T1232&quot;" data-cluster-id="16957" title="T1232: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Implementation plans specify how the goals of the strategic plan will be executed.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1232">Create implementation plan</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine domain and IP address space - T1250&quot;" data-cluster-id="16399" title="T1250: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Domain Names are the human readable names used to represent one or more IP addresses. IP addresses are the unique identifier of computing devices on a network. Both pieces of information are valuable to an adversary who is looking to understand the structure of a network. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1250">Determine domain and IP address space</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify job postings and needs/gaps - T1267&quot;" data-cluster-id="16446" title="T1267: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Job postings, on either company sites, or in other forums, provide information on organizational structure and often provide contact information for someone within the organization. This may give an adversary  information on people within the organization which could be valuable in social engineering attempts. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1267">Identify job postings and needs/gaps</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Dumpster dive - T1286&quot;" data-cluster-id="17446" title="T1286: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Dumpster diving is looking through waste for information on technology, people, and/or organizational items of interest. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1286">Dumpster dive</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify vulnerabilities in third-party software libraries - T1389&quot;" data-cluster-id="16382" title="T1389: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Many applications use third-party software libraries, often without full knowledge of the behavior of the libraries by the application developer. For example, mobile applications often incorporate advertising libraries to generate revenue for the application developer. Vulnerabilities in these third-party libraries could potentially be exploited in any application that uses the library, and even if the vulnerabilities are fixed, many applications may still use older, vulnerable versions of the library.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1389">Identify vulnerabilities in third-party software libraries</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Assess vulnerability of 3rd party vendors - T1298&quot;" data-cluster-id="16406" title="T1298: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Once a 3rd party vendor has been identified as being of interest it can be probed for vulnerabilities just like the main target would be.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1298">Assess vulnerability of 3rd party vendors</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Compromise 3rd party infrastructure to support delivery - T1312&quot;" data-cluster-id="16366" title="T1312: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Instead of buying, leasing, or renting infrastructure an adversary may compromise infrastructure and use it for some or all of the attack cycle.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1312">Compromise 3rd party infrastructure to support delivery</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Create backup infrastructure - T1339&quot;" data-cluster-id="16997" title="T1339: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Backup infrastructure allows an adversary to recover from environmental and system failures. It also facilitates recovery or movement to other infrastructure if the primary infrastructure is discovered or otherwise is no longer viable. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1339">Create backup infrastructure</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obtain Apple iOS enterprise distribution key pair and certificate - T1392&quot;" data-cluster-id="16354" title="T1392: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The adversary can obtain an Apple iOS enterprise distribution key pair and certificate and use it to distribute malicious apps directly to Apple iOS devices without the need to publish the apps to the Apple App Store (where the apps could potentially be detected).    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1392">Obtain Apple iOS enterprise distribution key pair and certificate</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Create infected removable media - T1355&quot;" data-cluster-id="16644" title="T1355: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Use of removable media as part of the Launch phase requires an adversary to determine type, format, and content of the media and associated malware. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1355">Create infected removable media</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test physical access - T1360&quot;" data-cluster-id="16894" title="T1360: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An  adversary can test physical access options in preparation for the actual attack. This could range from observing behaviors and noting security precautions to actually attempting access.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1360">Test physical access</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Upload, install, and configure software/tools - T1362&quot;" data-cluster-id="16423" title="T1362: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary may stage software and tools for use during later stages of an attack. The software and tools may be placed on systems legitimately in use by the adversary or may be placed on previously compromised infrastructure.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1362">Upload, install, and configure software/tools</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Exploit public-facing application - T1377&quot;" data-cluster-id="16687" title="T1377: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Exploit Public-Facing Application.**

The use of software, data, or commands to take advantage of a weakness in a computer system or program in order to cause unintended or unanticipated behavior. The weakness in the system can be a bug, a glitch, or a design vulnerability. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1377">Exploit public-facing application</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Unauthorized user introduces compromise delivery mechanism - T1387&quot;" data-cluster-id="16421" title="T1387: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Hardware Additions where appropriate.**

If an adversary can gain physical access to the target&#039;s environment they can introduce a variety of  devices that provide compromise mechanisms. This could include installing keyboard loggers, adding routing/wireless equipment, or connecting computing devices. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1387">Unauthorized user introduces compromise delivery mechanism</td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Create strategic plan - T1231&quot;" data-cluster-id="16923" title="T1231: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Strategic plans outline the mission, vision, and goals for an adversary at a high level in relation to the key partners, topics, and functions the adversary carries out.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1231">Create strategic plan</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine external network trust dependencies - T1259&quot;" data-cluster-id="16469" title="T1259: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Network trusts enable communications between different networks with specific accesses and permissions. Network trusts could include the implementation of domain trusts or the use of virtual private networks (VPNs).   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1259">Determine external network trust dependencies</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify people of interest - T1269&quot;" data-cluster-id="16638" title="T1269: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The attempt to identify people of interest or with an inherent weakness for direct or indirect targeting to determine an approach to compromise a person or organization.  Such targets may include individuals with poor OPSEC practices or those who have a trusted relationship with the intended target.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1269">Identify people of interest</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify business processes/tempo - T1280&quot;" data-cluster-id="16834" title="T1280: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Understanding an organizations business processes and tempo may allow an adversary to more effectively craft social engineering attempts or to better hide technical actions, such as those that generate network traffic.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1280">Identify business processes/tempo</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Research relevant vulnerabilities/CVEs - T1291&quot;" data-cluster-id="16838" title="T1291: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Common Vulnerability Enumeration (CVE) is a dictionary of publicly known information about security vulnerabilities and exposures. An adversary can use this information to target specific software that may be vulnerable.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1291">Research relevant vulnerabilities/CVEs</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;DNSCalc - T1324&quot;" data-cluster-id="17612" title="T1324: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use DNS Calculation.**

DNS Calc is a technique in which the octets of an IP address are used to calculate the port  for command and control servers from an initial DNS request.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1324">DNSCalc</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Domain registration hijacking - T1326&quot;" data-cluster-id="16972" title="T1326: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Domain Registration Hijacking is the act of changing the registration of a domain name without the permission of the original registrant. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1326">Domain registration hijacking</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Discover new exploits and monitor exploit-provider forums - T1350&quot;" data-cluster-id="16358" title="T1350: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An exploit takes advantage of a bug or vulnerability in order to cause unintended or unanticipated behavior to occur on computer hardware or software. The adversary may need to discover new exploits when existing exploits are no longer relevant to the environment they are trying to compromise. An adversary may monitor exploit provider forums to understand the state of existing, as well as newly discovered, exploits. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1350">Discover new exploits and monitor exploit-provider forums</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test signature detection for file upload/email filters - T1361&quot;" data-cluster-id="16363" title="T1361: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can test their planned method of attack against existing security products such as email filters or intrusion detection sensors (IDS). " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1361">Test signature detection for file upload/email filters</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Leverage compromised 3rd party resources - T1375&quot;" data-cluster-id="16473" title="T1375: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

The utilization of resources not owned by the adversary to launch exploits or operations. This includes utilizing equipment that was previously compromised or leveraging access  gained by other methods (such as compromising an employee at a business partner location). " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1375">Leverage compromised 3rd party resources</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Derive intelligence requirements - T1230&quot;" data-cluster-id="16882" title="T1230: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership or key decision makers may derive specific intelligence requirements from Key Intelligence Topics (KITs) or Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs).  Specific intelligence requirements assist analysts in gathering information to establish a baseline of information about a topic or question and collection managers to clarify the types of information that should be collected to satisfy the requirement.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1230">Derive intelligence requirements</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Determine firmware version - T1258&quot;" data-cluster-id="16990" title="T1258: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Firmware is permanent software programmed into the read-only memory of a device. As with other types of software, firmware may be updated over time and have multiple versions. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1258">Determine firmware version</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify personnel with an authority/privilege - T1271&quot;" data-cluster-id="16441" title="T1271: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Personnel internally to a company may have non-electronic specialized access, authorities, or privilege that make them an attractive target for an adversary.  One example of this is an individual with financial authority to authorize large transactions.  An adversary who compromises this individual might be able to subvert large dollar transfers. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1271">Identify personnel with an authority/privilege</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify business relationships - T1283&quot;" data-cluster-id="16975" title="T1283: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Business relationship information may be used by an adversary to shape social engineering attempts (exploiting who a target expects to hear from) or to plan for technical actions such as exploiting network trust relationship. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1283">Identify business relationships</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Research visibility gap of security vendors - T1290&quot;" data-cluster-id="16400" title="T1290: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

If an adversary can identify which security tools a victim is using they may be able to identify ways around those tools. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1290">Research visibility gap of security vendors</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Data Hiding - T1320&quot;" data-cluster-id="17338" title="T1320: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Certain types of traffic (e.g., DNS tunneling, header inject) allow for user-defined fields. These fields can then be used to hide data. In addition to hiding data in network protocols, steganography techniques can be used to hide data in images or other file formats. Detection can be difficult unless a particular signature is already known.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1320">Data Hiding</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Dynamic DNS - T1333&quot;" data-cluster-id="17448" title="T1333: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Dynamic DNS is a automated method to rapidly update the domain name system mapping of hostnames to IPs. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1333">Dynamic DNS</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify resources required to build capabilities - T1348&quot;" data-cluster-id="16413" title="T1348: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

As with legitimate development efforts, different skill sets may be required for different phases of an attack. The skills needed may be located in house, can be developed, or may need to be contracted out. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1348">Identify resources required to build capabilities</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Push-notification client-side exploit - T1373&quot;" data-cluster-id="16677" title="T1373: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

A technique to push an iOS or Android MMS-type message to the target which does not require interaction on the part of the target to be successful.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1373">Push-notification client-side exploit</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Develop KITs/KIQs - T1227&quot;" data-cluster-id="17286" title="T1227: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership derives Key Intelligence Topics (KITs) and Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs) from the areas of most interest to them.  KITs are an expression of management&#039;s intelligence needs with respect to early warning, strategic and operational decisions, knowing the competition, and understanding the competitive situation. KIQs are the critical questions aligned by KIT which provide the basis for collection plans, create a context for analytic work, and/or identify necessary external operations. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1227">Develop KITs/KIQs</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Discover target logon/email address format - T1255&quot;" data-cluster-id="16445" title="T1255: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Email addresses, logon credentials, and other forms of online identification typically share a common format. This makes guessing other credentials within the same domain easier. For example if a known email address is first.last@company.com it is likely that others in the company will have an email in the same format. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1255">Discover target logon/email address format</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify sensitive personnel information - T1274&quot;" data-cluster-id="16631" title="T1274: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary may identify sensitive personnel information not typically posted on a social media site, such as address, marital status, financial history, and law enforcement infractions. This could be conducted by searching public records that are frequently available for free or at a low cost online. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1274">Identify sensitive personnel information</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify job postings and needs/gaps - T1278&quot;" data-cluster-id="16447" title="T1278: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Job postings, on either company sites, or in other forums, provide information on organizational structure, needs, and gaps in an organization. This may give an adversary an indication of weakness in an organization (such as under-resourced IT shop). Job postings can also provide information on an organizations structure which could be valuable in social engineering attempts.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1278">Identify job postings and needs/gaps</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Test signature detection - T1292&quot;" data-cluster-id="16964" title="T1292: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can test the detections of malicious emails or files by using  publicly available services, such as virus total, to see if their files or emails cause an alert. They can also use similar services that are not openly available and don&#039;t publicly publish results or they can test on their own internal infrastructure. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1292">Test signature detection</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Domain Generation Algorithms (DGA) - T1323&quot;" data-cluster-id="16501" title="T1323: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Domain Generation Algorithms.**

The use of algorithms in malware to periodically generate a large number of domain names which function as rendezvous points for malware command and control servers.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1323">Domain Generation Algorithms (DGA)</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Install and configure hardware, network, and systems - T1336&quot;" data-cluster-id="16356" title="T1336: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary needs the necessary skills to set up procured equipment and software to create their desired infrastructure. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1336">Install and configure hardware, network, and systems</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obtain/re-use payloads - T1346&quot;" data-cluster-id="17055" title="T1346: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A payload is the part of the malware which performs a malicious action. The adversary may re-use payloads when the needed capability is already available. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1346">Obtain/re-use payloads</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Replace legitimate binary with malware - T1378&quot;" data-cluster-id="16488" title="T1378: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Replacing a legitimate binary with malware can be accomplished either by replacing a binary on a legitimate download site or standing up a fake or alternative site with the malicious binary. The intent is to have a user download and run the malicious binary thereby executing malware. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1378">Replace legitimate binary with malware</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Generate analyst intelligence requirements - T1234&quot;" data-cluster-id="16621" title="T1234: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analysts may receive Key Intelligence Topics (KITs) and Key Intelligence Questions (KIQs) from leadership or key decision makers and generate intelligence requirements to articulate intricacies of information required on a topic or question. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1234">Generate analyst intelligence requirements</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Enumerate client configurations - T1262&quot;" data-cluster-id="16961" title="T1262: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Client configurations information such as the operating system and web browser, along with additional information such as version or language, are often transmitted as part of web browsing communications.  This can be accomplished in several ways including use of a compromised web site to collect details on visiting computers.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1262">Enumerate client configurations</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify supply chains - T1265&quot;" data-cluster-id="16988" title="T1265: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Supply chains include the people, processes, and technologies used to move a product or service from a supplier to a consumer. Understanding supply chains may provide an adversary with opportunities to exploit the people, their positions, and relationships, that are part of the supply chain.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1265">Identify supply chains</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify supply chains - T1276&quot;" data-cluster-id="16991" title="T1276: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Supply chains include the people, processes, and technologies used to move a product or service from a supplier to a consumer. Understanding supply chains may provide an adversary with opportunities to exploit organizational relationships.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1276">Identify supply chains</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Dynamic DNS - T1311&quot;" data-cluster-id="17375" title="T1311: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Dynamic DNS is a method of automatically updating a name in the DNS system. Providers offer this rapid reconfiguration of IPs to hostnames as a service. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1311">Dynamic DNS</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obfuscate infrastructure - T1331&quot;" data-cluster-id="17394" title="T1331: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Obfuscation is hiding the day-to-day building and testing of new tools, chat servers, etc. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1331">Obfuscate infrastructure</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Post compromise tool development - T1353&quot;" data-cluster-id="16640" title="T1353: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

After compromise, an adversary may utilize additional tools to facilitate their end goals. This may include tools to further explore the system, move laterally within a network, exfiltrate data, or destroy data. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1353">Post compromise tool development</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Runtime code download and execution - T1395&quot;" data-cluster-id="16486" title="T1395: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

Many mobile devices are configured to only allow applications to be installed from the mainstream vendor app stores (e.g., Apple App Store and Google Play Store).  These app stores scan submitted applications for malicious behavior.  However, applications can evade these scans by downloading and executing new code at runtime that was not included in the original application package.      " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1395">Runtime code download and execution</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify analyst level gaps - T1233&quot;" data-cluster-id="16620" title="T1233: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analysts identify gap areas that generate a compelling need to generate a Key Intelligence Topic (KIT) or Key Intelligence Question (KIQ).   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1233">Identify analyst level gaps</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Enumerate externally facing software applications technologies, languages, and dependencies - T1261&quot;" data-cluster-id="16353" title="T1261: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Software applications will be built using different technologies, languages, and dependencies. This information may reveal vulnerabilities or opportunities to an adversary.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1261">Enumerate externally facing software applications technologies, languages, and dependencies</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Mine social media - T1273&quot;" data-cluster-id="16973" title="T1273: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary may research available open source information about a target commonly found on social media sites such as Facebook, Instagram, or Pinterest.  Social media is public by design and provides insight into the interests and potentially inherent weaknesses of a target for exploitation by the adversary. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1273">Mine social media</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obtain templates/branding materials - T1281&quot;" data-cluster-id="16837" title="T1281: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Templates and branding materials may be used by an adversary to add authenticity to social engineering message. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1281">Obtain templates/branding materials</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Fast Flux DNS - T1325&quot;" data-cluster-id="16970" title="T1325: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Fast Flux DNS.**

A technique in which a fully qualified domain name has multiple IP addresses assigned to it which are swapped with extreme frequency, using a combination of round robin IP address and short Time-To-Live (TTL) for a DNS resource record.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1325">Fast Flux DNS</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obtain booter/stressor subscription - T1396&quot;" data-cluster-id="16845" title="T1396: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Configure and setup booter/stressor services, often intended for server stress testing, to enable denial of service attacks.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1396">Obtain booter/stressor subscription</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Remote access tool development - T1351&quot;" data-cluster-id="16608" title="T1351: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A remote access tool (RAT) is a piece of software that allows a remote user to control a system as if they had physical access to that system. An adversary may utilize existing RATs, modify existing RATs, or create their own RAT. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1351">Remote access tool development</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Spear phishing messages with malicious attachments - T1367&quot;" data-cluster-id="16417" title="T1367: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Spearphishing Attachment.**

Emails with malicious attachments are designed to get a user to open/execute the attachment in order to deliver malware payloads. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1367">Spear phishing messages with malicious attachments</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify gap areas - T1225&quot;" data-cluster-id="16959" title="T1225: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Leadership identifies gap areas that generate a compelling need to generate a Key Intelligence Topic (KIT) or Key Intelligence Question (KIQ).  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1225">Identify gap areas</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify job postings and needs/gaps - T1248&quot;" data-cluster-id="16443" title="T1248: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Job postings, on either company sites, or in other forums, provide information on organizational structure and often provide contact information for someone within the organization. This may give an adversary  information on technologies within the organization which could be valuable in attack or provide insight in to possible security weaknesses or limitations in detection or protection mechanisms. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1248">Identify job postings and needs/gaps</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Host-based hiding techniques - T1314&quot;" data-cluster-id="16683" title="T1314: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Host based hiding techniques are designed to allow an adversary to remain undetected on a machine upon which they have taken action. They may do this through the use of  static linking of binaries, polymorphic code, exploiting weakness in file formats, parsers, or self-deleting code. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1314">Host-based hiding techniques</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Procure required equipment and software - T1335&quot;" data-cluster-id="16474" title="T1335: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary will require some physical hardware and software. They may only need a lightweight set-up if most of their activities will take place using on-line infrastructure. Or, they may need to build extensive infrastructure if they want to test, communicate, and control other aspects of their activities on their own systems. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1335">Procure required equipment and software</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Spear phishing messages with malicious links - T1369&quot;" data-cluster-id="16420" title="T1369: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Spearphishing Link.**

Emails with malicious links are designed to get a user to click on the link in order to deliver malware payloads.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1369">Spear phishing messages with malicious links</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Receive operator KITs/KIQs tasking - T1235&quot;" data-cluster-id="16560" title="T1235: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Analysts may receive intelligence requirements from leadership and begin research process to satisfy a requirement.  Part of this process may include delineating between needs and wants and thinking through all the possible aspects associating with satisfying a requirement. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1235">Receive operator KITs/KIQs tasking</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify security defensive capabilities - T1263&quot;" data-cluster-id="16623" title="T1263: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Security defensive capabilities are designed to stop or limit unauthorized network traffic or other types of accesses.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1263">Identify security defensive capabilities</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Misattributable credentials - T1322&quot;" data-cluster-id="17433" title="T1322: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The use of credentials by an adversary with the intent to hide their true identity and/or portray them self as another person or entity.  An adversary may use misattributable credentials in an attack to convince a victim that credentials are legitimate and trustworthy when this is not actually the case. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1322">Misattributable credentials</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;SSL certificate acquisition for domain - T1337&quot;" data-cluster-id="16475" title="T1337: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Certificates are designed to instill trust. They  include information about the key, information about its owner&#039;s identity, and the digital signature of an entity that has verified the certificate&#039;s contents are correct. If the signature is valid, and the person examining the certificate trusts the signer, then they know they can use that key to communicate with its owner. Acquiring a certificate for a  domain name similar to one that is expected to be trusted may allow an adversary to trick a user in to trusting the domain (e.g., vvachovia instead of Wachovia -- homoglyphs).  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1337">SSL certificate acquisition for domain</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Spear phishing messages with text only - T1368&quot;" data-cluster-id="16419" title="T1368: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Phishing where appropriate.**

Emails with text only phishing messages do not contain any attachments or links to websites. They are designed to get a user to take a follow on action such as calling a phone number or wiring money. They can also be used to elicit an email response to confirm existence of an account or user. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1368">Spear phishing messages with text only</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify supply chains - T1246&quot;" data-cluster-id="16980" title="T1246: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Supply chains include the people, processes, and technologies used to move a product or service from a supplier to a consumer. Understanding supply chains may provide an adversary with opportunities to exploit the technology or interconnections that are part of the supply chain.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1246">Identify supply chains</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Network-based hiding techniques - T1315&quot;" data-cluster-id="16684" title="T1315: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Technical network hiding techniques are methods of modifying traffic to evade network signature detection or to utilize misattribution techniques. Examples include channel/IP/VLAN hopping, mimicking legitimate operations, or seeding with misinformation. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1315">Network-based hiding techniques</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;SSL certificate acquisition for trust breaking - T1338&quot;" data-cluster-id="16412" title="T1338: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Fake certificates can be acquired by legal process or coercion. Or, an adversary can trick a Certificate Authority into issuing a certificate. These fake certificates can be used as a part of Man-in-the-Middle attacks. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1338">SSL certificate acquisition for trust breaking</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Targeted client-side exploitation - T1371&quot;" data-cluster-id="16685" title="T1371: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

A technique used to compromise a specific group of end users by taking advantage of flaws in client-side applications. For example, infecting websites that members of a targeted group are known to visit with the goal to infect a targeted user&#039;s computer.    " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1371">Targeted client-side exploitation</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify technology usage patterns - T1264&quot;" data-cluster-id="16629" title="T1264: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Technology usage patterns include identifying if users work offsite, connect remotely, or other possibly less restricted/secured access techniques. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1264">Identify technology usage patterns</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Non-traditional or less attributable payment options - T1316&quot;" data-cluster-id="16379" title="T1316: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Using alternative payment options allows an adversary to hide their activities. Options include crypto currencies, barter systems, pre-paid cards or shell accounts. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1316">Non-traditional or less attributable payment options</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Shadow DNS - T1340&quot;" data-cluster-id="17348" title="T1340: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

The process of gathering domain account credentials in order to silently create subdomains pointed at malicious servers without tipping off the actual owner.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1340">Shadow DNS</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Targeted social media phishing - T1366&quot;" data-cluster-id="16648" title="T1366: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Spearphishing via Service.**

Sending messages through social media platforms to individuals identified as a target. These messages may include malicious attachments or links to malicious sites or they may be designed to establish communications for future actions.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1366">Targeted social media phishing</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Identify web defensive services - T1256&quot;" data-cluster-id="16633" title="T1256: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

An adversary can attempt to identify web defensive services as CloudFlare, IPBan, and Snort. This may be done by passively detecting services, like CloudFlare routing, or actively, such as by purposefully tripping security defenses. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1256">Identify web defensive services</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;OS-vendor provided communication channels - T1390&quot;" data-cluster-id="16504" title="T1390: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Google and Apple provide Google Cloud Messaging and Apple Push Notification Service, respectively, services designed to enable efficient communication between third-party mobile app backend servers and the mobile apps running on individual devices. These services maintain an encrypted connection between every mobile device and Google or Apple that cannot easily be inspected and must be allowed to traverse networks as part of normal device operation. These services could be used by adversaries for communication to compromised mobile devices.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1390">OS-vendor provided communication channels</td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Use multiple DNS infrastructures - T1327&quot;" data-cluster-id="16624" title="T1327: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A technique used by the adversary similar to Dynamic DNS with the exception that the use of multiple DNS infrastructures likely have whois records. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1327">Use multiple DNS infrastructures</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Unconditional client-side exploitation/Injected Website/Driveby - T1372&quot;" data-cluster-id="16502" title="T1372: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

A technique used to compromise victims wherein the victims visit a compromised website that redirects their browser to a malicious web site, such as an exploit kit&#039;s landing page.  The exploit kit landing page will probe the victim&#039;s operating system, web browser, or other software to find an exploitable vulnerability to infect the victim.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1372">Unconditional client-side exploitation/Injected Website/Driveby</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Map network topology - T1252&quot;" data-cluster-id="16960" title="T1252: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

A network topology is the arrangement of the various elements of a network (e.g., servers, workstations, printers, routers, firewalls, etc.). Mapping a network allows an adversary to understand how the elements are connected or related.  " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1252">Map network topology</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obfuscate infrastructure - T1309&quot;" data-cluster-id="17354" title="T1309: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Obfuscation is hiding the day-to-day building and testing of new tools, chat servers, etc. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1309">Obfuscate infrastructure</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Untargeted client-side exploitation - T1370&quot;" data-cluster-id="16680" title="T1370: &#10;**This technique has been deprecated. Please see ATT&amp;CK&#039;s Initial Access and Execution tactics for replacement techniques.**

A technique that takes advantage of flaws in client-side applications without targeting specific users. For example, an exploit placed on an often widely used public web site intended for drive-by delivery to whomever visits the site. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1370">Untargeted client-side exploitation</td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Mine technical blogs/forums - T1257&quot;" data-cluster-id="16842" title="T1257: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Technical blogs and forums provide a way for technical staff to ask for assistance or troubleshoot problems. In doing so they may reveal information such as operating system (OS), network devices, or applications in use. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1257">Mine technical blogs/forums</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obfuscate operational infrastructure - T1318&quot;" data-cluster-id="16938" title="T1318: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Obfuscation is hiding the day-to-day building and testing of new tools, chat servers, etc. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1318">Obfuscate operational infrastructure</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obtain domain/IP registration information - T1251&quot;" data-cluster-id="16558" title="T1251: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

For a computing resource to be accessible to the public, domain names and IP addresses must be registered with an authorized organization.   " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1251">Obtain domain/IP registration information</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obfuscate or encrypt code - T1319&quot;" data-cluster-id="16611" title="T1319: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Obfuscation is the act of creating code that is more difficult to understand. Encoding transforms the code using a publicly available format. Encryption transforms the code such that it requires a key to reverse the encryption. " tabindex="0" aria-label="T1319">Obfuscate or encrypt code</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td></tr><tr><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Spearphishing for Information - T1397&quot;" data-cluster-id="17015" title="T1397: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

Spearphishing for information is a specific variant of spearphishing. Spearphishing for information is different from other forms of spearphishing in that it it doesn&#039;t leverage malicious code. All forms of spearphishing are elctronically delivered social engineering targeted at a specific individual, company, or industry. Spearphishing for information is an attempt to trick targets into divulging information, frequently credentials, without involving malicious code. Spearphishing for information frequently involves masquerading as a source with a reason to collect information (such as a system administrator or a bank) and providing a user with a website link to visit. The given website often closely resembles a legitimate site in appearance and has a URL containing elements from the real site. From [...]" tabindex="0" aria-label="T1397">Spearphishing for Information</td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td style="border: none;"></td><td class="heatCell matrix-interaction " data-score="0" data-tag_name="misp-galaxy:mitre-attack-pattern=&quot;Obfuscation or cryptography - T1313&quot;" data-cluster-id="16932" title="T1313: &#10;This object is deprecated as its content has been merged into the enterprise domain. Please see the PRE matrix for its replacement. The prior content of this page has been preserved here.

